Package: taskhealthd
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Linux thread health monitoring daemon
 TaskHealth is a client-daemon thread health monitor for Linux user-space,
 inspired by QNX HAM. It detects unexpected thread exits, futex deadlocks,
 and lock-wait timeouts across multiple processes.
 .
 This package contains the taskhealthd daemon.

Package: libtaskhealth0
Architecture: linux-any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Linux thread health monitoring client library
 TaskHealth client library linked into business processes. Communicates
 with taskhealthd via Unix domain socket (SOCK_SEQPACKET) to register
 threads, send heartbeats, and receive alerts.
 .
 This package contains the shared library.

Package: libtaskhealth-dev
Architecture: linux-any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libtaskhealth0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Linux thread health monitoring library (development files)
 TaskHealth client library development files.
 .
 This package contains the static library, shared library symlink,
 pkg-config file, and header files.

Package: taskhealth-demo
Architecture: linux-any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libtaskhealth0
Description: Linux thread health monitoring (demo program)
 TaskHealth demo demonstrating auto-name, unexpected exit, deadlock,
 normal heartbeat, and lock-wait timeout scenarios.
